# Aside: new window only

Edgeways localhost UI uses Orca's embedded browser first
(`.cursor/rules/orca-browser.mdc`). This rule is for Aside when you
must use it.

When using Aside or the browser, never take over Sam's active session,
focused window, or existing tabs. Always open a new window for agent work.

## Do

- Open a fresh window with `openTab(url)` (or `aside exec` that creates a
  new window) and stay in that window.
- `listBrowserTabs()` is allowed to inspect what is open without attaching.
- Attach to an existing tab only if Sam explicitly names that tab and asks
  you to use it.

## Do not

- Call `attachActiveBrowserTab()`.
- Attach to or navigate a tab in his focused/active window.
- Resume or steer his live Aside session with `--session` unless he asked
  to continue that session.
- Drive personal tabs that happen to be open (Rightmove, email, shopping).
